  "texts": {
    "preamble": "Brajmohan Rajawat vs Madhya Pradesh Through Shri Brajesh ... on 21 November, 2025 Author: Gurpal Singh Ahluwalia Bench: G. S. Ahluwalia Neutral Citation No. 2025:Mphc-Gwl:30977 1 In The High Court Of Madhya Pradesh At Gwalior Before Hon'Ble Shri Justice G. S. Ahluwalia On The 21st Of November, 2025 Miscellaneous Second Appeal No. 19 of 2025 Brajmohan Rajawat Versus Madhya Pradesh Through Shri Brajesh Kumar Shiromani Khady Suraksha Adhikari Prashasan Appearance: Shri Ashish Singh Jadon, Advocate for applicant. Shri S.S.Kushwah, Government Advocate for respondent/State Order",
    "facts": "2. Facts necessary for disposal of present appeal, in short, are that a complaint was filed against appellant on the allegation that on 18/7/2023, the dairy belonging to appellant was inspected and sample of loose curd and loose milk-mix was collected. The curd was found to be of substandard quality. Copy of report of the Food Analyst was sent to the appellant with an information that he can file an appeal under section 46(4) of FSSA and under rule 2.4.2(6) of Food Safety and Standard Rules, 2011 but no appeal was filed. Being aggrieved by the order passed by the Adjudicating Officer, appellant filed an appeal which too has been dismissed by IX District Judge, Gwalior in RCA No.39/2025.",
    "arguments": "5. A solitary ground has been raised by counsel for appellant that penalty amount may be further reduced. 6. Sale of substandard food articles is detrimental to the mankind.",
    "petitioner_arguments": "5. A solitary ground has been raised by counsel for appellant that penalty amount may be further reduced. 6. Sale of substandard food articles is detrimental to the mankind.",
